-failed":"Payout request failed. Please try again or contact support.","verform-ub-accepted-docs-title":"Accepted documents","verform-ub-accepted-docs-subtitle":"Upload any one of these — dated within the last 3 months.","verform-ub-accepted-docs-subtitle-company":"Upload a company bank statement or official letter — dated within the last 3 months.","verform-ub-doc-utility-title":"Utility bill","verform-ub-doc-bank-title":"Bank statement","verform-ub-doc-letter-title":"Official letter","verform-ub-see-example":"See example →","verform-ub-requirements-title":"Your document must show","verform-ub-req-name":"Full name","verform-ub-req-address":"Address matching the form above","verform-ub-req-date":"Issue date within the last 3 months","verform-ub-example-modal-got-it":"Got it","verform-ub-example-modal-hint":"Your document must show your name, address, and a date within the last 3 months.","verform-ub-example-modal-utility-title":"Utility bill — example","verform-ub-example-modal-bank-title":"Bank statement — example","verform-ub-example-modal-letter-title":"Official letter — example","terms-update-disagree":"Disagree and leave","age-check-warning-animal":"We detected what appears to be an animal in your media. Content featuring animals isn't allowed on xfree.","age-check-warning-underage":"Someone in your media appears to be under 18.","btn-select-thumbnail":fY,"btn-edit-thumbnail":"Change cover","btn-add-thumbnail":"Add cover","use-timeline-to-select-thumbnail":"Drag the timeline to pick your cover frame. Drag main image to set cover position.","btn-set-thumbnail":fY,"cover-required":"Add a cover before you post","cover-preview-label":"Cover","btn-set-thumbnail-isset":"Cover set","cr2-hero-title":"Your fans are here.\u003Cbr\u003EThey just haven’t found \u003Cem\u003Eyou\u003C\u002Fem\u003E yet.","cr2-hero-sub":"xfree sends free traffic to your links — and pays you every Sunday for the content people actually watch. No paywall. No cut of your subs. \u003Cspan class=\"hl\"\u003EJust reach.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E","cr2-hero-cta":"I want free traffic","cr2-hero-suffix":"2,400+ creators get paid every Sunday","cr2-pola-1":"upload day 🎬","cr2-pola-2":"content is live 😛","cr2-pola-3":"sunday cha-ching 💸","cr2-alt-pola-1":"Creator setting up her ring light","cr2-alt-pola-2":"Scrolling the feed","cr2-alt-pola-3":"Creator checking her Sunday earnings","cr2-alt-pola-4":"Checking the phone at midnight","cr2-ticker-earnings":"weekly earnings","cr2-ticker-payout":"payout sent","cr2-ticker-referral":"referral bonus","cr2-ticker-contest":"contest reward","cr2-how-kick":"How it works","cr2-how-title":"It’s \u003Cem\u003Estupidly\u003C\u002Fem\u003E simple.","cr2-how-1-t":"1. Upload your stuff","cr2-how-1-d":"Takes ~30 seconds. Drop your links in.","cr2-how-2-t":"2. We put it in the feed","cr2-how-2-d":"People watch, like, share — and click your links.","cr2-how-3-t":"3. Sunday: cha-ching","cr2-how-3-d":"All of that turns into money. Every week.","cr2-how-hand":"that’s it. that’s the business model. ✍️","cr2-stats-kick":fZ,"cr2-stats-title":"How much traffic? \u003Cem\u003EThis much.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","cr2-stat-1":"views on an average xfree video","cr2-stat-2":"of viewers click the creator’s link","cr2-stat-3":"clicks on an average link","cr2-stats-cap":"Measured across all of xfree.","cr2-money-kick":"The money","cr2-money-title":"Sunday \u003Cem\u003ECha-Ching\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. 🔔","cr2-money-sub":"Watch time, likes, shares and link clicks build your score all week. Sunday at midnight, the weekly pool is split between verified creators. Higher score, bigger share.","cr2-fact-1-k":"Earnings land","cr2-fact-1-v":"Every \u003Cem\u003ESunday\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, midnight","cr2-fact-2-k":"First payout","cr2-fact-2-v":"From \u003Cem\u003E$100\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","cr2-fact-3-k":"Top creators make","cr2-fact-3-v":W,"cr2-fact-4-k":"Your subs & PPV — we take nothing","cr2-fact-4-v":"100% \u003Cem\u003Eyours\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","cr2-money-pola-cap":"midnight check 🌙","cr2-sunday-kick":"meanwhile, every single week…","cr2-sunday-title":"Sunday. \u003Cem\u003EMidnight.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","cr2-sunday-date":"Sunday night","cr2-sunday-t1":"Tuesday","cr2-sunday-t2":"Sunday 00:01","cr2-sunday-n1":"Your post is \u003Cb\u003Elive\u003C\u002Fb\u003E! 🎬","cr2-sunday-n2":"First week done. \u003Cb\u003E+$46\u003C\u002Fb\u003E earned.","cr2-sunday-n3":"People loved it. \u003Cb\u003E+$134\u003C\u002Fb\u003E earned.","cr2-sunday-n4":"You’re on fire. \u003Cb\u003E+$303\u003C\u002Fb\u003E earned.","cr2-sunday-payout-label":X,"cr2-sunday-payout-sub":"On its way to your account 🎉","cr2-sunday-sub":"Weekly earnings land every Sunday at midnight. Payout whenever you hit $100 and ask for it.","cr2-split-1":"The weekly pool —","cr2-split-2":"is just the \u003Cem\u003Estart\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","cr2-bonus-kick":"Bonuses","cr2-bonus-title":"Cash \u003Cem\u003Eon top\u003C\u002Fem\u003E of the pool.","cr2-bonus-1-t":"Contests & boosted pay","cr2-bonus-1-d":"Monthly contests and boosted-pay campaigns. Extra cash for the content we’re pushing.","cr2-bonus-2-t":"Referral bonus · $50","cr2-bonus-2-d":"Know another creator? Bring her in. Verified & posting? $50 — just message the team.","cr2-bonus-custom-name":"Big audience?","cr2-bonus-custom-val":"Custom deal","cr2-bonus-custom-d":"Big name? Big offer. Negotiated 1-on-1, always.","cr2-bonus-custom-li1":f_,"cr2-bonus-custom-li2":"Dedicated manager","cr2-product-kick":"The product","cr2-product-title":"Upload in 30 seconds.\u003Cbr\u003EEdit like a \u003Cem\u003Epro\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","cr2-product-1-t":"Online editor","cr2-product-1-d":"Trim, crop, flip horizontal to vertical — right in the browser.","cr2-product-2-t":fP,"cr2-product-2-d":"Caption, tags and categories – written automatically for you.","cr2-product-3-t":"30-second upload","cr2-product-3-d":"Drop the file, add your links, done.","cr2-product-4-t":"Priority review","cr2-product-4-d":"Verified creators jump the approval queue.","cr2-product-hand-1":"runs in the browser — no app needed ✍️","cr2-product-hand-2":"Studio Assist fills it in — skip or edit anytime ✍️","cr2-alt-editor":"The real xfree upload editor","cr2-alt-ai":"Studio Assist writes the caption, tags and category during upload","cr2-verify-kick":"Verification","cr2-verify-title":"Verified means \u003Cem\u003Epaid\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","cr2-verify-sub":"One-time thing. Takes minutes. Unlocks the money.","cr2-verify-1-t":"ID + selfie","cr2-verify-1-when":"day one","cr2-verify-1-d":"Encrypted, checked by a real human.","cr2-verify-2-t":fU,"cr2-verify-2-when":"at $50 earned","cr2-verify-2-d":"Done before your first $100 payout.","cr2-verify-3-t":"Payout details","cr2-verify-3-when":"once, forever","cr2-verify-3-d":"Add once. Paid every time.","cr2-verify-pola-cap":"the famous ID selfie 🤳","cr2-verify-stamp":"Verified ✓","cr2-verify-note":"nobody knows it’s you — unless you want them to 💜","cr2-alt-verify":"Creator laughing while taking the classic ID verification selfie, card blown out by the flash","cr2-tg-kick":"Community","cr2-tg-title":"The party is on \u003Cem\u003ETelegram\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. 🎉","cr2-tg-news-t":"Announcements","cr2-tg-badge-pub":"public","cr2-tg-news-d":"Everything worth money, posted here first.","cr2-tg-news-btn":"Join @xfreenews","cr2-tg-lounge-t":"Creators’ lounge","cr2-tg-badge-priv":"invite only","cr2-tg-lounge-d":"Private group for creators with our team inside.","cr2-tg-lounge-s1":F,"cr2-tg-lounge-s2":"Verify & earn","cr2-tg-lounge-s3":f$,"cr2-tg-lounge-s4":f$,"cr2-tg-lounge-btn":"Start earning — get invited","cr2-faq-kick":ga,"cr2-faq-title":gb,"cr2-faq-1-q":gc,"cr2-faq-1-a":"Yes. Uploading is free and the traffic is free. You get paid — not the other way around.","cr2-faq-2-q":"Do you take a cut of my OnlyFans?","cr2-faq-2-a":"No. Never. Your links, your subs, your money. xfree pays \u003Cem\u003Eyou\u003C\u002Fem\u003E — not the other way around.","cr2-faq-3-q":"How do I actually get the money?","cr2-faq-3-a":"Verify once. Earnings land in your wallet every Sunday at midnight. From $100 you can request your first payout (after that, from $300) — SEPA, PayPal, Paxum or bank wire.","cr2-faq-4-q":"What’s the catch?","cr2-faq-4-a":"There isn’t one. Great content makes xfree bigger, and the weekly reward pool keeps great content coming. That’s the whole deal.","cr2-faq-5-q":"What can I upload?","cr2-faq-5-a":"Your own adult content — solo, couples, whatever you make. It has to be yours, and everyone in it must be 18+ and consenting. Short vertical clips tend to do best.","cr2-final-title":"Sunday is payday.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cem\u003EBe there.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","cr2-final-sub":"Create your account, verify, upload. The next pool splits this Sunday at midnight.","cr2-final-btn":"Start earning — it’s free","cr2-final-suffix":"Signing up is the fastest part.","cr2-tg-news-what":"What lands here","cr2-tg-news-r1":"Bonus pay campaigns","cr2-tg-news-r2":"Contests & winners","cr2-tg-news-r3":"New feature drops","cr2-tg-lounge-sub":"invites from the team","cr2-tg-lounge-how":"How to get in","cr2-faq-6-q":"What is xfree, anyway?","cr2-faq-6-a":"A free adult tube — watching costs nothing, there’s no paywall. We earn on ads, and every week we split a reward pool between verified creators based on what people actually watched. Your links ride along for free.","cr2-faq-7-q":"Can I upload videos I already have?","cr2-faq-7-a":"Absolutely — it’s the smartest way to start. Take clips you already made for other platforms, trim them in the editor and post. Nothing new to shoot.","cr2-faq-8-q":"Will anyone know it’s me?","cr2-faq-8-a":"Only if you want them to. You post under any name you like, and your ID is seen only by the compliance team — it never appears on the site.","menu-earn-videos":"Get paid for your videos","menu-partner-tag":gd,"ag2-hero-hand":"for OF management agencies 👔","ag2-hero-title":"You buy traffic.\u003Cbr\u003EWe \u003Cem\u003Egive it away\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","ag2-hero-sub":"Bring your whole roster under one master account, put your models’ links in front of 50 million monthly visitors — and get paid for every verified creator you bring. \u003Cspan class=\"hl\"\u003EZero media spend.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E","ag2-cta-register":ge,"ag2-cta-meeting":"Schedule a meeting","ag2-flow-sub":"monthly visitors on xfree","ag2-flow-badge":"1.5M+ every single day","ag2-flow-cap":"Free organic traffic, straight to your models’ pages — wherever they earn.","ag2-flow-aria":"xfree traffic flowing to your models’ links across networks","ag2-stats-kick":fZ,"ag2-stats-title":"Reach you’d normally \u003Cem\u003Epay for\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","ag2-stat-1":"visitors a month","ag2-stat-2":"of them arrive from Google search","ag2-stat-3":"views on an average video","ag2-stat-4":"of viewers click the model’s link","ag2-stats-cap":"Google Analytics, last 30 days. Your roster plugs straight into it.","ag2-why-kick":"Why xfree","ag2-why-title":"Marketing is your biggest cost.\u003Cbr\u003EWe just \u003Cem\u003Edeleted\u003C\u002Fem\u003E it.","ag2-why-1-t":"Free, measurable traffic","ag2-why-1-d":"Organic reach for every model on the roster from day one. No ad account, no bids, no budget caps.","ag2-why-2-t":"No shadowbans. Ever.","ag2-why-2-d":"We’re an adult platform. Post uncensored — no burner accounts, no bans, no blurring.","ag2-why-3-t":"Zero extra production","ag2-why-3-d":"The clips your team already cuts for socials work here as-is. Same content, one more funnel.","ag2-onb-kick":"One master account","ag2-onb-title":"Your whole roster.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cem\u003EOne login.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ag2-onb-1-t":ge,"ag2-onb-1-d":"One master account for the agency. Every creator you bring gets linked under it.","ag2-onb-2-t":"Link your creators","ag2-onb-2-d":"Each model passes her own KYC — it’s personal by design, that’s what keeps payouts clean. Once she’s verified, her account links under your master and you switch between profiles without logging out.","ag2-onb-3-t":"Upload & earn","ag2-onb-3-d":"Content goes live after priority review. Sunday earnings show which model converts.","ag2-roster-queued":"verifying","ag2-roster-verified":"linked","ag2-roster-more":"+ 12 more","ag2-res-kick":"Measurable results","ag2-res-title":"Know which model \u003Cem\u003Econverts\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","ag2-res-1-t":"Your links, your tracking","ag2-res-1-d":"Every post carries the model’s links. Use your own tracked URLs and attribute every OF signup in your stack.","ag2-res-2-t":"Earnings are the scoreboard","ag2-res-2-d":"Weekly earnings follow watch time, likes, shares and link clicks. The models that earn are the models that convert.","ag2-res-3-t":"Roster summaries","ag2-res-3-d":"Your account manager sends roster performance summaries — numbers, not vibes.","ag2-rm-title":"Weekly roster summary","ag2-rm-sub":"from your account manager","ag2-deal-kick":"The deal","ag2-deal-title":"We pay \u003Cem\u003Eyou\u003C\u002Fem\u003E to join.","ag2-deal-1-name":"Per verified creator","ag2-deal-1-d":"Every model you bring who passes KYC puts $50 in the agency’s pocket. Paid after her first 20 approved posts.","ag2-deal-2-name":"On signup","ag2-deal-2-val":"Launch bonus","ag2-deal-2-d":"Every new agency starts with one — sized with your account manager on the call.","ag2-deal-3-name":"Big roster?","ag2-deal-3-val":f_,"ag2-deal-3-d":"The whole deal is negotiable. That’s what the meeting is for.","ag2-reach-kick":"Extra reach","ag2-reach-title":"We run the \u003Cem\u003Espotlight\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","ag2-reach-sub":"Organic reach is the baseline — every model on the roster gets that for free. When one of them deserves more eyes, one message to your account manager turns these on:","ag2-reach-note":"Ami has the marker — just ask ✍️","ag2-reach-1-t":"Featured playlists","ag2-reach-1-d":"Her clips, slotted into the curated playlists people actually scroll.","ag2-reach-2-t":"Paid promo posts","ag2-reach-2-d":"A boosted post that puts her profile in front of the whole feed.","ag2-reach-3-t":"Site banners","ag2-reach-3-d":"Prime placement across xfree — her face on the busiest pages.","ag2-reach-4-t":"Blog feature","ag2-reach-4-d":"A dedicated article on the xfree blog. Good for her, good for search.","ag2-part-kick":"Partnership","ag2-part-title":"A \u003Cem\u003Epartner\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, not a platform.","ag2-mc-name":"Ami 👋","ag2-mc-sub":"your onboarding manager","ag2-mc-btn":"Schedule a meeting with Ami","ag2-mc-alt":"Ami, your onboarding manager, at his desk","ag2-part-1-t":"Dedicated account manager","ag2-part-1-d":"A real human who knows your roster by name. Direct line, not a ticket queue.","ag2-part-2-t":"Private Telegram group","ag2-part-2-d":"Agencies and top creators — early access to bonuses, features and campaigns.","ag2-faq-kick":ga,"ag2-faq-title":gb,"ag2-faq-1-q":"Who gets paid what?","ag2-faq-1-a":"Your call. Run the roster under the agency’s company account (KYB) and payouts go to the agency — or let each model collect her own. We set it up together during onboarding.","ag2-faq-2-q":"What does it cost?","ag2-faq-2-a":"Nothing. No fee, no rev-share, no cut of your OF revenue. We grow when your models bring their audience.","ag2-faq-3-q":"Is exclusivity required?","ag2-faq-3-a":"No. xfree is another traffic source on top of what you already run — not a replacement. Keep posting everywhere.","ag2-faq-4-q":"Do we manage the creator accounts?","ag2-faq-4-a":"Yes — one master account with every creator linked under it. Switch between profiles without logging out. You handle the content, we handle the traffic.","ag2-faq-5-q":"What do you need from us?","ag2-faq-5-a":"Each model completes her own identity verification (KYC) — the same one every creator on xfree goes through, and it takes minutes. Once she’s verified, we link her account under your master.","ag2-faq-6-q":"How fast do posts go live?","ag2-faq-6-a":"Agency uploads get priority review — most content is live within a day.","ag2-faq-7-q":"Is extra promotion included?","ag2-faq-7-a":"Yes — playlists, promo posts, banners and blog features are available to every agency, whenever you need them. Tell your account manager which model to push and it gets scheduled.","ag2-faq-8-q":"Do the models need to shoot anything new?","ag2-faq-8-a":"No. The feed runs on content they already have — clips and trailers that are already earning elsewhere can pull traffic here too.","ag2-final-title":"Bring the roster.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cem\u003EWe’ll bring the traffic.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ag2-final-sub":"Or book 20 minutes with your account manager and we’ll walk you through the numbers.","ag2-final-suffix":"Registration takes minutes. The meeting takes 20.","ag2-band-q":"Are you a creator?","ag2-band-link":"Here’s your deal →","cr2-agencies-band-q":"Managing multiple creators?","cr2-agencies-band-link":"xfree for agencies →","menu-agencies":"For agencies","meta-agencies-title":"xfree for Agencies — Free Traffic for Your Whole Roster","meta-agencies-subtitle":"Onboard your roster in one flow, put your models in front of 50 million monthly visitors and get paid for every verified creator you bring. Zero media spend.",Agencies:"Agencies","account-switch-failed":"Account switch failed. Please try again.","settings-email-prefs-roster-report":"Weekly roster report","payout-info-for-paypal":"Requires a PayPal Business account. Personal accounts are not supported.","verify-softblock-title":"Get seen. Get paid.","verify-softblock-desc":"Verified creators get full reach, more views, and real weekly earnings. Unverified accounts stop at 10 posts — verify now and forget the limit.","verify-softblock-btn-verify":U,"verify-softblock-btn-continue":l,"verify-hardblock-title":"You've reached the maximum of uploaded posts","verify-hardblock-desc":"That's the max for unverified accounts. Verify once and you're unlimited — plus your posts go live with full reach and start earning every week.","verify-hardblock-btn":U,"video-thumbnail-missing":"Please select a cover image first.","video-chapter-tag-missing":"With multiple scenes, every scene must have at least one tag.","meta-academy-title":"xfree Academy — learn to make AI images that earn","meta-academy-subtitle":"A free course in generating AI images. Write a prompt, look at what came back, change one word, run it again.","label-current-password":"Current password","label-new-email":"New e-mail address","settings-email-in-use":"This e-mail is already in use","settings-email-change-request":"Request e-mail change","settings-email-change-confirm":"Confirm e-mail change","verifypopup-add-link-header":"\u003Ch2\u003ELinks need a verified account\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EHere's what verifying unlocks.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E","verifypopup-add-link-content":"\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EYour links go live\u003C\u002Fstrong\u003E\n\u003Cspan\u003ENew links work right away, and hidden ones in older posts come back.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fli\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EClicks pay you\u003C\u002Fstrong\u003E\n\u003Cspan\u003ELink clicks build your weekly score and your payout.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fli\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EDone in minutes\u003C\u002Fstrong\u003E\n\u003Cspan\u003EAn ID and a selfie is all we need.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fli\u003E\n\u003C\u002Ful\u003E","verify-email-popup-header":"Your email isn't confirmed yet","verify-email-popup-content":"Likes, comments, follows, uploads and downloads are locked until you click the link we sent to","verify-email-popup-resend":"Resend confirmation email","settings-email-change-no-password":"You sign in with Google or Apple, so there's no password on the account yet. Set one {securityLink} and you can change your email right here.","settings-email-change-no-password-link":"in Security","settings-email-change-note":"We'll send a confirmation link to the new address. Your current email stays active until you open it.","settings-email-change-sent":"We've sent a confirmation link to your new address — it can take a few minutes to arrive. Open it and the change is done.","settings-email-wrong-password":"Wrong password.","settings-email-change-already-sent":"The confirmation link is already in your new inbox — check spam too. You can ask for a new one in 12 hours.","ac1-hero-kick":"xfree academy · chapter 01 of 03","ac1-hero-h1":"Make AI images people \u003Cem\u003Epay to see\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.","ac1-hero-lead":"A free course from xfree: learn to make AI NSFW content and earn with it — on xfree or anywhere else. Chapter 01 is images, with Grok Imagine as the first tool. No experience, nothing to install.","ac1-hero-cta1":"See an example first","ac1-hero-cta1-o":"Back to the chapter","ac1-hero-cta2":"Log in — it's free","ac1-hero-img-alt":"AI-generated portrait made in Grok Imagine — the kind of image chapter 01 teaches you to prompt","ac1-fact-1-k":"This chapter","ac1-fact-1-v":"9 parts · 2–3 hours with the tool open","ac1-fact-2-k":"The course","ac1-fact-2-v":"Free with your xfree login · similar courses sell for $70–150","ac1-fact-3-k":"Tools","ac1-fact-3-v":"$0 to try · about $30\u002Fmo once you post daily","ac1-fact-4-k":"Top xfree creators make","ac1-fact-4-v":W,"ac1-rm-kick":"one course, three chapters","ac1-rm-h":"Three chapters. \u003Cem\u003EImages, video, payday.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-rm-now":"you are here","ac1-rm-1":"AI images with Grok and Seedream","ac1-rm-1-d":"Write a prompt that works, fix one detail, take her from topless to full nudity.","ac1-rm-2":"From a still into video","ac1-rm-2-d":"Turn the images you kept into short clips that move.","ac1-rm-3":"Publishing and getting paid","ac1-rm-3-d":"Post on xfree, build a page, turn views into payouts.","ac1-r-kick":"the warm-up","ac1-r-h":"Write a good prompt.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cem\u003EGet exactly what you want.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-r-lead":"Two prompts, both “correct” — the tool happily takes either one. The difference is who decides what the photo looks like: you, or the model. Click both and compare.","ac1-r-src":"Grok Imagine output","ac1-r-promptlab":"Which prompt","ac1-r-t0":"the model chose","ac1-r-t1":"you chose","ac1-r-v1":"\u003Cb\u003ESix decisions, none of them yours.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Her age, her body, her hair, the place, the light, the mood — the prompt says nothing about them, so the model picked all six for you.","ac1-r-v2":"\u003Cb\u003EThe same six, all yours.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Nothing changed but the words. Knowing which words is the whole course.","ac1-r-img-alt":"Grok Imagine output from the two-word prompt, four results the model chose on its own","ac1-ch-kick":"chapter 01 · ai images with grok and seedream","ac1-ch-h":"Your first image. \u003Cem\u003EThen the same again, on your own.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-ch-lead":"That's the goal of this chapter: a process you can repeat, not one lucky photo. Nine parts, each a few minutes, and you try every one of them right here on the page — you type the prompt, the page tells you which block you left out.","ac1-ch-p1":"\u003Cb\u003EBy the end you know:\u003C\u002Fb\u003E","ac1-ch-li1":"how a prompt turns into an image, and why the same words never repeat","ac1-ch-li2":"how to fix one detail without losing the woman","ac1-ch-li3":"which Grok settings matter, what it costs, and when to hand the image to a second tool","ac1-ch-p2":"Everything after this chapter is tuning: better results out of the same four blocks, and more detail inside them.","ac1-side-label":"Parts of chapter 01","ac1-side-g1":"Writing a prompt","ac1-side-g2":"More from one image","ac1-side-g3":"Tools and cost","ac1-rd-done":"{n} of {t} done","ac1-blocks-nav":"The four blocks","ac1-layers-nav":"Building it in layers","ac1-edit-nav":"Fixing one detail","ac1-rerun-nav":"Why runs differ","ac1-series-nav":"One image, a series","ac1-fix-nav":"When it won't listen","ac1-tool-nav":"The Grok interface","ac1-cost-nav":gf,"ac1-seedream-nav":"Full nudity with Seedream","ac1-side-locked":"log in to open","ac1-side-done":"done","ac1-side-soon":"coming","ac1-part-kick":"part {n} of {t}","ac1-part-kick-free":"part {n} of {t} · open to everyone","ac1-part-next":"Next · part {n}","ac1-part-next-locked":"Log in to open part {n}","ac1-part-last":"Finish the chapter","ac1-ck-k":"quick check","ac1-ck-pick":gg,"ac1-toc-kick":"parts 2–9","ac1-toc-h":"Part 1 was free. \u003Cem\u003ESo are the other eight.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-toc-lead":"Log in and parts 2 to 9 open on this page: layers, edits, cost, and Seedream for full nudity.","ac1-toc-login":"Log in and open parts 2–9","ac1-toc-free":"Any xfree account. No card, no download.","ac1-toc-unlock":"Unlock part {n}","ac1-blocks-h":"A prompt is four blocks","ac1-blocks-wl":"The four blocks every working prompt is built from.","ac1-blocks-lead":"Every prompt that works is built from the same four blocks: subject, setting, style and details. Once you can see them, you can also see what was missing from every prompt that disappointed you.","ac1-blocks-p1":"\u003Cb\u003EA prompt is just a description.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E There is no secret phrase and no magic formula, and nobody is holding back the words that make it work. A weak prompt and a strong one differ in one thing only, and that is how much of the picture you decided yourself. Everything you leave out, the model fills in for you, and it fills it in with whatever it has seen most.","ac1-blocks-do":"Click a block to switch it off, and see which decision you just handed back to the model.","ac1-blocks-legend-k":"what each block decides","ac1-blk-subject-label":"Subject","ac1-blk-subject-what":"Who is in the picture, and every detail of her: age, body, hair, clothes.","ac1-blk-subject-miss":"\u003Cb\u003ENo subject detail.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E The model picks her age, body, hair and clothes for you.","ac1-blk-setting-label":"Setting","ac1-blk-setting-what":"Where it happens.","ac1-blk-setting-miss":"\u003Cb\u003ENo setting.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E She ends up somewhere generic: a studio, a bedroom, wherever the model leans.","ac1-blk-style-label":"Style","ac1-blk-style-what":"How the picture should look as a picture: photo, film, illustration, grain.","ac1-blk-style-miss":"\u003Cb\u003ENo style.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E You get the model’s house look. Glossy, retouched, obviously AI.","ac1-blk-detail-label":"Details","ac1-blk-detail-what":"Light, mood, colour, camera angle.","ac1-blk-detail-miss":"\u003Cb\u003ENo details.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Light, colour and the angle are left to chance.","ac1-blocks-bridge":"You know what each block does. Now the words that go in them.","ac1-blocks-ex-why-k":"why this block matters","ac1-blocks-ex-why-subject":"Subject is the only block that decides who she is. Leave it thin and every run brings a different woman.","ac1-blocks-ex-why-setting":"Setting is what makes a feed look lived-in instead of shot against a blank wall.","ac1-blocks-ex-why-style":"Style decides whether anyone believes the photo. It is the difference between a render and a snapshot.","ac1-blocks-ex-why-detail":"Light and angle are what separate a photo somebody took from an image a model produced.","ac1-blocks-take-k":j,"ac1-blocks-take-1":"A prompt is four blocks: subject, setting, style, details.","ac1-blocks-take-2":"Whatever you leave out of them, the model decides for you.","ac1-blocks-take-3":"When a result disappoints you, ask which block is thin before you rewrite anything.","ac1-blocks-take-4":"None of this is a secret phrase. It is a description, written on purpose.","ac1-blocks-bl-n0":"When a result disappoints you, one of these four is almost always the one you left out.","ac1-blocks-bl-n-empty":"\u003Cb\u003ENothing left to work from.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E With an empty prompt every run is a different random picture.","ac1-blocks-bl-cap-full":"all four blocks · the strong prompt","ac1-blocks-bl-cap-miss":"run without","ac1-blocks-bl-cap-empty":"no prompt · pure noise","ac1-blocks-ex-k":"what to write in each block","ac1-blocks-ex-lead":"Knowing the four blocks is half of it, and the other half is vocabulary. Here are five ways to fill each one — click any phrase and it swaps into the prompt behind this photo.","ac1-blocks-ex-cap-base":"the strong prompt · nothing swapped","ac1-blocks-ex-cap":"one block swapped · {block}","ac1-blocks-doctor":"Now write one yourself. Paste a prompt into the Doctor below — your own, or one you already ran in Grok — and it names the block you left out and tells you what to add.","ac1-d-kick":"part 1 checkpoint · your own prompt","ac1-d-h":"Get it right \u003Cem\u003Eon the first go.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-d-lead":"This is where you find out whether your own prompt holds up. Type one in, or paste one you already ran in Grok, and the Doctor checks all four blocks, names the one that is missing, and rewrites the prompt for you if you ask.","ac1-d-in-k":"Your prompt","ac1-d-preset-k":"or start from one of these","ac1-d-preset-vague":gh,"ac1-d-preset-negation":"negation","ac1-d-preset-overloaded":"overloaded","ac1-d-preset-strong":"strong","ac1-d-placeholder":"Write or paste your prompt here — English, plain sentences.","ac1-d-img-alt":"Grok Imagine output from the prompt in the box","ac1-d-clear":"clear","ac1-d-missing":"missing","ac1-d-of4":"of 4 blocks","ac1-d-words":"words","ac1-d-warn-styles":"{n} looks at once","ac1-d-warn-vague":gh,"ac1-d-cap-strong":"one run of this exact prompt","ac1-d-cap-illu":"where this kind of prompt lands","ac1-d-cap-idle":"nothing run yet","ac1-d-cap-over":"one prompt, four runs — a different style wins each time","ac1-d-cap-neg":"“no tattoos” — the model heard “tattoos”","ac1-d-fx-empty":"Write a prompt above, or start from one of the four below.","ac1-d-fx-lang":"Write the prompt in English. The models are trained on it, and everything else is a translation they have to guess at.","ac1-d-fx-vague":"\u003Ccode\u003E{w}\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E tells the model nothing. Everyone pictures something else, the model included. Say what you mean: age, body, hair, clothes.","ac1-d-fx-short":"Too short. Whatever you leave out, the model invents.","ac1-d-fx-subject":"No subject detail. Add age, body type, hair and clothes.","ac1-d-fx-setting":"No setting. Say where the scene happens, or the model picks somewhere generic.","ac1-d-fx-mj":"Those \u003Ccode\u003E--parameters\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E are Midjourney syntax. Grok reads them as words. Delete them and set the ratio in the UI instead.","ac1-d-fx-weight":"That weight syntax is from Stable Diffusion. Grok has no \u003Ccode\u003E(word:1.2)\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E and no brackets — it reads them as text. Write it as a sentence.","ac1-d-fx-vague2":"One word to cut: \u003Ccode\u003E{w}\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E. The model can't picture it, so it just spends attention. Everything else here works.","ac1-d-fx-neg":"Negation barely works. The model reads \u003Ccode\u003Eno\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E and \u003Ccode\u003Enot\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E as the thing itself. Describe the state you want instead — part 6 has the swaps.","ac1-d-fx-boost":"\u003Ccode\u003E{w}\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E does nothing here. Those are leftovers from older image models. Spend the words on the four blocks instead.","ac1-d-fx-styles":"{n} different looks at once — photo, film and illustration pull against each other. The model quietly picks one and drops the rest. Keep the one you want.","ac1-d-fx-style":"No style. Add \u003Ccode\u003Ecandid photo\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Eshot on film\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E or \u003Ccode\u003Eshot on smartphone\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E. That is what stops it looking like stock AI.","ac1-d-fx-long":"Too long. The model cannot tell what matters. Cut it back to the four blocks.","ac1-d-fx-detail":"All four blocks are nearly there. Add light: \u003Ccode\u003Esoft morning light\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Egolden hour\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E. Light is most of what makes a photo believable.","ac1-d-fx-ok":"Solid. All four blocks are there. Go generate — that is a prompt you can post from.","ac1-d-ai-go":"Rewrite my prompt","ac1-d-ai-login":"Log in to rewrite it","ac1-d-ai-wait":"Rewriting…","ac1-d-ai-off":"The rewrite didn't come back. Try again.","ac1-d-rw-k":"your prompt, rewritten","ac1-d-rw-en":"Prompts stay in English — that's what the models are trained on.","ac1-d-rw-open":"Open Grok Imagine","ac1-d-rw-more":"That is one prompt fixed. Parts 2 to 9 are how you write the next one without help.","ac1-d-rw-more-a":"Log in — they open on this page","ac1-layers-h":"Build the prompt in layers","ac1-layers-wl":"Build one prompt in six passes and walk away with it written down.","ac1-layers-lead":"One prompt, built in six passes. You add a layer, generate, and compare the result with the run before it — that is how you find out what a single word actually does.","ac1-layers-p1":"You already know the four blocks. A layer is one pass at the prompt, and each pass fills in a little more of one block, so six layers and four blocks are not two systems — they are the same prompt seen twice. Generate after every layer and compare, because a word only teaches you something when it is the only thing that changed.","ac1-layers-do":"Start at layer one and work down. Generate at each step, then compare it with the run before.","ac1-layers-p2":"You generate, you look, you change one word and you generate again, and most of what you make gets thrown away. Beginners burn more images than anyone, because you are still learning what each word does — that is not a sign you are bad at this, it is how the people who do this for a living work too.","ac1-layers-p2-h":"Your first image is never the finished one","ac1-layers-take-1":"Build the prompt in layers, in this order: subject, setting, style, details.","ac1-layers-take-2":"Generate after every layer and compare, or you never learn what the word did.","ac1-layers-take-3":"A natural look comes from words like \u003Ci\u003Enatural\u003C\u002Fi\u003E, \u003Ci\u003Ecandid\u003C\u002Fi\u003E, \u003Ci\u003Eno makeup\u003C\u002Fi\u003E and \u003Ci\u003Eamateur\u003C\u002Fi\u003E.","ac1-layers-take-4":"When you tune a prompt that already works, change one thing and leave the rest alone.","ac1-layers-goal":"The goal is a real young woman rather than a retouched catalogue face: Swedish, around 25, big natural breasts, sitting on a bench outdoors.","ac1-layers-l1-cap":"layer 1 · the subject","ac1-layers-l1-say":"Bare on purpose. Usable, and completely random: the model picked her age, her face, the bench and the frame. \u003Cb\u003EWhat you don’t say, the model decides.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E","ac1-layers-l2-cap":"layer 2 · who she is","ac1-layers-l2-say":"\u003Cb\u003Enatural face, no makeup, casual everyday clothes\u003C\u002Fb\u003E drag the model away from the retouched look it defaults to. Still too polished? Add \u003Ci\u003Ecandid photo, amateur photo\u003C\u002Fi\u003E.","ac1-layers-l3-cap":"layer 3 · the setting","ac1-layers-l3-say":"She was sitting “on a bench”. But where? Compare it with the previous round. \u003Cb\u003EEvery layer takes one more decision away from the model.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E","ac1-layers-l4-cap":"layer 4 · style and mood","ac1-layers-l4-say":"\u003Cb\u003Ecandid photo\u003C\u002Fb\u003E is the word that matters here. It asks for a moment instead of a pose. \u003Cb\u003Eshot on smartphone\u003C\u002Fb\u003E finishes the job: this now reads as a photo somebody actually took.","ac1-layers-l5-cap":"layer 5 · topless","ac1-layers-l5-say":"Three words: \u003Cb\u003Eshe is topless\u003C\u002Fb\u003E. Nothing else moved. That is what building in layers buys you. \u003Cb\u003EEvery tool has its own limits on what it will render.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E","ac1-layers-l6-cap":"layer 6 · swap one word","ac1-layers-l6-say":"\u003Cb\u003EOne swap, not a rewrite.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E soft morning light became \u003Cb\u003Eevening, warm street lights\u003C\u002Fb\u003E. Everything else stays. Too polished? \u003Ci\u003Ecandid, no makeup\u003C\u002Fi\u003E. Too close? \u003Ci\u003Efull body shot\u003C\u002Fi\u003E.","ac1-layers-gen":"Generate","ac1-layers-again":gi,"ac1-layers-next":"Add a layer","ac1-layers-badge":"layer {n} of {t}","ac1-layers-nostack":"the model decides","ac1-layers-recipe-k":"your recipe","ac1-layers-recipe-hint":"Work through all six layers and the finished prompt is yours to copy.","ac1-layers-stamp":"your prompt is unlocked","ac1-layers-steps-group":"Prompt layers","ac1-layers-take-k":j,"ac1-layers-ck1-q":"You add a layer and the photo gets worse. What now?","ac1-layers-ck1-w1":"Rewrite the whole prompt","ac1-layers-ck1-ok":"Remove that layer and run again","ac1-layers-ck1-w2":"Add three more layers","ac1-layers-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EOne layer changed, so only one layer can be the cause.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Take it out, run again, then try different words for it.","ac1-layers-ck1-no":"That throws away five layers that were working.","ac1-rerun-h":"The model never sees a picture","ac1-rerun-wl":"Why the same words never return the same photo, and how to use that.","ac1-rerun-lead":"There is no photo library behind the button. The model imagines your prompt fresh every single run, which is why the same words never return the same photo twice.","ac1-rerun-p1":"The model does not see anything. It estimates the most probable result of your words, starting from visual noise and sharpening it pass by pass until an image appears. So two identical prompts returning two different women is not a bug — that is the mechanism, and once you expect it you stop fighting it.","ac1-rerun-do":"Run the same prompt five times and watch who shows up.","ac1-rerun-pull":"The cheapest better image is the prompt you already have, run again.","ac1-rerun-take-k":j,"ac1-rerun-take-1":"Every run starts from fresh noise, so nothing is remembered between runs.","ac1-rerun-take-2":"Everything you leave open in the prompt gets rolled again each time.","ac1-rerun-take-3":"Ten runs of a working prompt beat one run of a rewritten one.","ac1-rerun-same":"one prompt · {n} runs","ac1-rerun-src":"same prompt, every run","ac1-rerun-roll":gi,"ac1-rerun-run":"run {n}","ac1-rerun-hand":"four runs is nothing. ten is normal, and you keep two.","ac1-rerun-r1":"\u003Cb\u003ERun 1.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Perfectly usable, but is she the woman you meant? Run it again and see who shows up instead.","ac1-rerun-n2":"\u003Cb\u003EA different photo every run.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E The process is probabilistic, not exact.","ac1-rerun-done":"\u003Cb\u003E{n} runs, {n} different women, one prompt.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Notice how loose those {w} words are. Everything you leave open, the model rolls for. Click the thumbnails to compare.","ac1-rerun-pipe-k":"What happens after you press generate","ac1-rerun-pipe-1":"Grok splits your prompt into words.","ac1-rerun-pipe-2":"It turns those words into visual meanings it learned from millions of photos.","ac1-rerun-pipe-3":"It starts from visual noise, not from a picture.","ac1-rerun-pipe-4":"It sharpens that noise step by step, each pass a little clearer.","ac1-rerun-pipe-5":"Your image emerges out of it — same words, fresh noise, a different photo.","ac1-rerun-m2":"Run it unchanged ten times and pick the best one, because the prompt already works and you are only rolling more dice. Then save the keeper's prompt somewhere — in a month you will not remember a word of it.","ac1-rerun-ck1-q":"Same prompt, second run, a different woman. Why?","ac1-rerun-ck1-w1":"The model avoids repeating itself","ac1-rerun-ck1-w2":"The prompt is too long","ac1-rerun-ck1-ok":"Every run starts from fresh noise","ac1-rerun-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EFresh noise every time.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E There is no memory between runs, so whatever the prompt leaves open gets rolled again.","ac1-rerun-ck1-no":"There is no memory between runs, and length is not what changes her.","ac1-series-h":"One good image is a series","ac1-series-wl":"Turn one image that worked into a week of posts.","ac1-series-lead":"One image that works is worth ten that nearly do. Instead of starting again, leave the scene alone and move the camera, or swap exactly one thing in it.","ac1-series-p1":"\u003Cb\u003EA prompt that works is a recipe.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E You do not throw a recipe away to cook something else — you change one ingredient. Swap the setting, or the clothes, or the light, and she stays who she was, which is what makes a feed look like one person instead of a folder of strangers.","ac1-series-do":"Pick a mode below, then click through the terms and watch what stays the same.","ac1-series-take-k":j,"ac1-series-take-1":"Change the frame and you get a new photo of the same moment.","ac1-series-take-2":"Add one framing term at the end of the prompt: \u003Ccode\u003Eclose-up portrait\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Efull body shot\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Eshot from behind\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E.","ac1-series-take-3":"Swap one thing per round, so every result tells you something.","ac1-series-take-4":"Six terms on one working prompt is six posts.","ac1-series-mode1":"Change the frame","ac1-series-mode2":"Change one thing","ac1-series-mode-group":"What to change","ac1-series-shot-closeup-g":"the face only","ac1-series-shot-medium-g":"waist up","ac1-series-shot-full-g":"whole body","ac1-series-shot-wide-g":"her in the place","ac1-series-shot-behind-g":"from the back","ac1-series-shot-low-g":"camera below her","ac1-series-cat-camera":"camera","ac1-series-cat-setting":"setting","ac1-series-cat-light":"light","ac1-series-variants":"{n} variants","ac1-series-hand":"one scene that worked can carry a whole week of posts.","ac1-series-m2":"Add one framing term to the end of the prompt — \u003Ccode\u003Eclose-up portrait\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Efull body shot\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003Eshot from behind\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E. Six terms, six photos of one moment, and that is what a consistent feed is made of.","ac1-series-m2-h":"Move the camera, not the scene","ac1-series-ck1-q":"You swapped the café for a forest and changed the light. The photo broke. Which one did it?","ac1-series-ck1-w1":"The café","ac1-series-ck1-w2":"The light","ac1-series-ck1-ok":"Can't tell — two swaps at once","ac1-series-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003ETwo changes, one result.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E The cause is hidden. One swap per round, and every result tells you something.","ac1-series-ck1-no":"Maybe — but you changed two things, so this one result cannot tell you which.","ac1-edit-h":"Fix one detail, keep the woman","ac1-edit-wl":"Change one detail in a finished photo without losing the woman in it.","ac1-edit-lead":"The photo is almost right and one thing is off. You do not have to roll the dice again — upload it back into Grok and say what to change, and everything you liked about it stays.","ac1-edit-p1":"Regenerating rolls the whole image again, so you get a new face, new light and a new pose along with the fix. An edit touches only the spot you name. The rule of thumb is simple: if several things are wrong, regenerate, and if one thing is wrong, edit it.","ac1-edit-do":"Switch between the two versions below. The prompt underneath is the whole edit — one sentence.","ac1-edit-take-k":j,"ac1-edit-take-1":"Edit when one thing is wrong, and write a new prompt when several are.","ac1-edit-take-2":"An edit changes only what you name and leaves the rest of the pixels alone.","ac1-edit-take-3":"Write the change as one sentence, and make one change per round.","ac1-edit-m2":"Open the image in Imagine, or drop it in with the + in the prompt bar, then write the change as one plain sentence — \u003Ccode\u003Echange the background to a city street\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E, or \u003Ccode\u003Eremove the object in the background\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E — and generate.","ac1-edit-m2-h":"How you do it in Grok","ac1-edit-m3":"If you ask for the background and the shorts in the same breath, you will not know which of them broke her face. Make one change, look at it, then make the next.","ac1-edit-m3-h":"Change one thing per round","ac1-edit-hand":"one detail off? edit it. half the photo wrong? cheaper to start over.","ac1-edit-ui-cap":"Grok Imagine · the bench woman from part 2, after one edit. Bench, pose and light stayed.","ac1-edit-ui-alt":"Grok Imagine with an uploaded image and an edit prompt in the bar","ac1-edit-t0":"before","ac1-edit-t1":"after one edit","ac1-edit-t0-cap":"the Grok run this started from","ac1-edit-k":"the edit","ac1-edit-src":"Grok Imagine · upload + edit","ac1-edit-cap":"uploaded photo + “{term}”","ac1-edit-ck1-q":"The photo is right except for a lamp in the background. What do you do?","ac1-edit-ck1-w1":"Regenerate until it's gone","ac1-edit-ck1-ok":"Upload it back: remove the lamp in the background","ac1-edit-ck1-w2":"Add “no lamp” and regenerate","ac1-edit-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EOne detail wrong is an edit.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E The woman, the light and the pose stay exactly where they are.","ac1-edit-ck1-no":"Regenerating re-rolls her face, and “no lamp” reads as “lamp”.","ac1-fix-h":"When the model won't listen","ac1-fix-wl":"Five rewrites, in order, for when the model returns something else.","ac1-fix-lead":"The prompt is written well, everything makes sense, and the model still returns something else. Five moves, in the order you should try them.","ac1-fix-p1":"It generates what is probable from your words, so if you write \u003Ccode\u003Ewoman on a beach\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E you get the million retouched beach shots it has seen. It is not ignoring you — that is simply what “beach plus woman” looks like statistically, and once you know that, you stop arguing with the model and start steering it.","ac1-fix-p1-h":"The model does not generate your idea","ac1-fix-do":"Click any row to see why the swap works. Try them from the top — the first four cost you nothing.","ac1-fix-take-k":j,"ac1-fix-take-1":"Say the same thing differently rather than saying it louder.","ac1-fix-take-2":"Name the state you want, because negation barely registers.","ac1-fix-take-3":"Move the detail that matters to the front of the prompt.","ac1-fix-take-4":"When a prompt starts drifting, roll back to the last version that worked.","ac1-fix-take-5":"If four rewrites have not fixed one detail, edit the image instead.","ac1-fix-mod":"Sometimes the prompt is not the problem. Every tool moderates content, Grok included, so some requests will not pass and others come back consistently off. That is a limit of the tool, not of your skill.","ac1-fix-sw-k":"in this order","ac1-fix-sw1-k":"Say it differently","ac1-fix-sw1-why":"Repeating a word adds no weight. A different phrase pulls from a different part of what the model knows.","ac1-fix-sw2-k":"Name the state you want","ac1-fix-sw2-why":"Negation barely registers. The model paints the words it sees, and it saw “smiling”.","ac1-fix-sw3-k":"Move it to the front","ac1-fix-sw3-no":"the detail sits at the end of a long prompt","ac1-fix-sw3-yes":"the same detail in the first words","ac1-fix-sw3-why":"The start of the prompt carries more weight. The last detail sometimes doesn’t make the cut.","ac1-fix-sw4-k":"Roll back","ac1-fix-sw4-no":"five more edits on a prompt that is drifting","ac1-fix-sw4-yes":"the last version that worked, plus one change","ac1-fix-sw4-why":"Every edit adds something. Eventually the words contradict each other. That is why you save working prompts.","ac1-fix-sw5-k":"Edit, don’t regenerate","ac1-fix-sw5-no":"ten more generations for one bad detail","ac1-fix-sw5-yes":"upload it back into Imagine and fix that spot","ac1-fix-sw5-why":"Same move as part 3. It sits last because the four above cost you nothing.","ac1-fix-ax-t":"cheapest · try this first","ac1-fix-ax-b":"last resort · costs you a re-upload","ac1-fix-hand":"you will reach for move 4 more often than you expect. keep every prompt that worked.","ac1-fix-ui-cap":"move 5 · that + is where the image goes back in","ac1-fix-ui-alt":"The prompt bar in Grok Imagine, with the upload button circled","ac1-fix-beat":"your turn · 3 rounds","ac1-fix-fx-h":"Which wording actually works?","ac1-fix-fx-lead":"Each of these prompts has one word that fights the model. Pick the swap that fixes it.","ac1-fix-fx1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EThe model paints the words it sees\u003C\u002Fb\u003E — and it saw “smiling”. Give it the state you want instead.","ac1-fix-fx1-no":"Still the same word — the model still sees “smile”.","ac1-fix-fx2-why":"\u003Cb\u003ENegation barely registers.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Describe the scene you want, not the one you don’t.","ac1-fix-fx2-no":"That is still a negation — the model mostly hears “city” \u002F “buildings”.","ac1-fix-fx3-why":"\u003Cb\u003ERepeating a word adds nothing.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E A different phrase pulls from a different part of what the model knows.","ac1-fix-fx3-no":"Louder is not different — repetition does not add weight.","ac1-fix-fx-score":"{n} of {t} fixed","ac1-fix-fx-round":"round {n}","ac1-fix-fx-ask":gg,"ac1-fix-fx-solved":"fixed","ac1-fix-fx-locked":"finish round {n} first","ac1-fix-fx-done":"that is the move that works on everything from here on — you describe what you want instead of forbidding what you do not.","ac1-fix-fx-done-clean":"three for three, no misses. you are now officially harder to confuse than the model.","ac1-tool-h":"The whole tool, in seven spots","ac1-tool-wl":"Every control in Grok Imagine that changes your result.","ac1-tool-lead":"Grok Imagine has seven controls worth knowing, and none of them hide in a settings menu. All the real power sits in the prompt, which is why the six parts before this one were about words.","ac1-tool-do":"The seven spots are numbered on the screenshot. Click a number to zoom in on it.","ac1-tool-hs1-t":"New Generation","ac1-tool-hs1-b":"Starts a fresh image. Grok also has a plain chat; everything in this course happens on the Imagine side.","ac1-tool-hs2-t":"The prompt field","ac1-tool-hs2-b":"Describe it the way you would to a person. There are no commands to learn.","ac1-tool-hs3-t":"Image \u002F Video","ac1-tool-hs3-b":"Pick before you generate. This chapter is images; video is chapter 02.","ac1-tool-hs4-t":"Speed \u002F Quality","ac1-tool-hs4-b":"Quality is slower and better. Speed is fine for first tries, since you throw most of them away.","ac1-tool-hs5-t":"Aspect ratio","ac1-tool-hs5-b":"The open menu is this button. 9:16 for stories and reels, 1:1 for a grid, 2:3 for portraits.","ac1-tool-hs6-t":"Upload your own","ac1-tool-hs6-b":"Drop in a photo or an earlier generation. That is where the edits from part 3 go back in, and later where a still becomes a video.","ac1-tool-hs7-t":aD,"ac1-tool-hs7-b":"Everything you generate stays in your library. Like it first, then come back and download it any time.","ac1-tool-ratio-k":"Pick the ratio before you generate","ac1-tool-take-k":j,"ac1-tool-take-1":"Set the aspect ratio before you generate, never after.","ac1-tool-take-2":"Quality is slower and better; Speed is fine for first tries you plan to throw away.","ac1-tool-take-3":"Create a free account at grok.com, open Imagine, and build your first prompt there.","ac1-tool-ui-alt":"The Grok Imagine screen, with seven numbered spots","ac1-tool-ratio-lead":"Set the ratio before you generate rather than cropping afterwards, because an image composed in its own format always beats one trimmed into it. Each photo below was generated in the format under it.","ac1-tool-ratio-916-l":"9:16 vertical","ac1-tool-ratio-916-g":"stories · reels · TikTok","ac1-tool-ratio-11-l":"1:1 square","ac1-tool-ratio-11-g":"the feed grid","ac1-tool-ratio-23-l":"2:3 portrait","ac1-tool-ratio-23-g":"classic photo portrait","ac1-tool-ratio-169-l":"16:9 wide","ac1-tool-ratio-169-g":"YouTube covers · web","ac1-tool-ratio-32-l":"3:2 landscape","ac1-tool-ratio-32-g":"wider shots · scenery","ac1-tool-m1":"A download icon sits under every result and saves it as a PNG or a JPEG. Everything you generate also stays in your library, so you can like it now and come back for it any time — and the library is far easier to browse on a computer than on a phone.","ac1-tool-dl-alt":"The download icon under a finished result in Grok Imagine","ac1-tool-dl-cap":"Grok Imagine · the download icon sits under every result","ac1-tool-m1-h":"Saving and finding your images","ac1-tool-ck1-q":"When do you set the aspect ratio?","ac1-tool-ck1-ok":"Before generating","ac1-tool-ck1-w1":"After, by cropping","ac1-tool-ck1-w2":"Grok reads it from the prompt","ac1-tool-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EBefore.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E An image generated in its ratio beats a cropped one every time.","ac1-tool-ck1-no":"Cropped loses the composition, and the prompt doesn't set the ratio.","ac1-cost-h":gf,"ac1-cost-wl":"What the tools actually cost and which plan you need to start.","ac1-cost-lead":"Grok is a subscription and WaveSpeed is pay per image. The free tiers will cover your first afternoon, but posting daily needs a plan.","ac1-cost-p1":"Making AI images costs money, and that is fair rather than a scam: these models run on serious computing power and every image you generate spends some of it. While you are only trying things out you can stay on the free tiers. Once you want to work without waiting for tomorrow, a subscription is unavoidable.","ac1-cost-take-k":j,"ac1-cost-take-1":"Start on SuperGrok at $30 a month. It is the first plan that lets you actually work.","ac1-cost-take-2":"You will burn the most images in month one, so budget for that month rather than for month six.","ac1-cost-take-3":"The free tier and Lite are for touching the tool, and you outgrow both sooner than you expect.","ac1-cost-take-4":"Monthly buys you freedom, yearly buys you a discount. Think one tool ahead.","ac1-cost-n-k":"you need","ac1-cost-n1":gj,"ac1-cost-n1-d":"Generation. There is a free tier for trying it and a monthly plan for working.","ac1-cost-n2":"WaveSpeed","ac1-cost-n2-d":"Edits and full nudity. You pay per image out of prepaid credit, with no subscription.","ac1-cost-n3":"Any device","ac1-cost-n3-d":"A phone is enough to follow along, though a computer makes everything easier.","ac1-cost-q1-q":"Why these two?","ac1-cost-q1":"Two tools learned properly beat five sites half-learned, and Grok and WaveSpeed carry every chapter of this course. That is why we stay with them instead of chasing whatever launched this week.","ac1-cost-q2-q":"Want a free first try?","ac1-cost-q2":"Gemini generates images free through models like Nano Banana Pro, and ChatGPT Plus generates them inside the chat you already pay for. Both are fine for a first look and poor for real work: less control over the result, no usable history, and limits that stop you mid-session. That is the reason this course stays on two tools instead of five.","ac1-cost-plan-k":"which grok plan","ac1-cost-plan-lead":"Four tiers, and only volume decides which one you need. Slide to how much you plan to generate in a month.","ac1-cost-mo":"\u002Fmo","ac1-cost-pl1-cap":"~10 images every 2 hours","ac1-cost-pl1-say":"\u003Cb\u003EFree is for touching the tool, not for working.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Ten images, then a two-hour wait — and one good photo costs you ten tries.","ac1-cost-pl2-cap":"~20 images a day","ac1-cost-pl2-say":"\u003Cb\u003ELite gets you further, then holds you back:\u003C\u002Fb\u003E around twenty a day and lower quality. You outgrow it sooner than you expect.","ac1-cost-pl3-cap":"~50 images a day","ac1-cost-pl3-say":"\u003Cb\u003EStart here.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Around fifty a day is enough to actually work. It slows down after roughly 35 in one sitting, but it does not stop you.","ac1-cost-pl4-cap":"~200 images a day","ac1-cost-pl4-say":"\u003Cb\u003EOnly for all-day generating.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E Around two hundred a day and no throttling. You are not starting here.","ac1-cost-slider":"images per month","ac1-cost-keep":"At roughly three keepers out of ten tries, {n} generations means about \u003Cb\u003E{k}\u003C\u002Fb\u003E images worth posting.","ac1-cost-note":"Limits move, and xAI does not publish exact numbers. Check your own account before you buy.","ac1-cost-shot-alt":"SuperGrok pricing page","ac1-cost-hand":"month one burns the most images. budget for that one, not for month six.","ac1-cost-pull":"Pay for a year up front and you are betting a year on one tool. These models get replaced in months.","ac1-cost-q3-q":"Monthly or yearly?","ac1-cost-q3":"SuperGrok yearly is $300, roughly 17% under twelve monthly payments. Go monthly while you are still deciding and yearly once you know you will stay, because these tools change fast and a year is a long commitment.","ac1-cost-ck1-q":"How does WaveSpeed charge you?","ac1-cost-ck1-w1":"A monthly subscription","ac1-cost-ck1-ok":"Per image, from prepaid credit","ac1-cost-ck1-w2":"Nothing","ac1-cost-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EPer image.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E You top up credit and every generation takes a few cents off it. No plan to cancel.","ac1-cost-ck1-no":"No plan and no free ride — credit, spent per generation.","ac1-seedream-h":"Grok stops at topless. Seedream finishes.","ac1-seedream-wl":"Take a topless Grok photo all the way to full nudity.","ac1-seedream-lead":"Grok builds the scene. Seedream 5.0 Pro, a ByteDance edit model, changes only what you name in a finished image. Upload the Grok photo, write one sentence, download.","ac1-seedream-two-k":"why two tools","ac1-seedream-two-1-h":gj,"ac1-seedream-two-1":"Fast generation, cheap iteration. Use it to find the woman, the scene and the frame.","ac1-seedream-two-2-h":"Seedream 5.0 Pro","ac1-seedream-two-2":"Made for editing rather than for starting from nothing. It changes only what you name and leaves the rest of the pixels alone, it can work with more than one reference at a time, it holds detail up to print resolution — and it renders full nudity.","ac1-seedream-steps-k":"grok, then wavespeed · six steps","ac1-seedream-s1-h":"Make the image in Grok","ac1-seedream-s1":"Everything from parts 1 to 7 applies. Pick the best run and download it at full size.","ac1-seedream-s2-h":"Sign in at wavespeed.ai","ac1-seedream-s2":"Google or GitHub, one click. No card; every new account starts with $1 of credit.","ac1-seedream-s3-h":"Top Up your credit","ac1-seedream-s3":"Account menu, top right, then Top Up. Credit never expires and can't be refunded, so start small.","ac1-seedream-s4-h":"Find the model","ac1-seedream-s4":"Search \u003Ccode\u003Eseedream 5.0 pro\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E. Open the one ending in \u003Ccode\u003E\u002Fedit\u003C\u002Fcode\u003E — image-to-image, not text-to-image.","ac1-seedream-s5-h":"Upload and edit","ac1-seedream-s5":"Drop in the Grok image (1), write the change (2), set 9:16 (3), 2k (4), jpeg (5). Generate.","ac1-seedream-s6-h":K,"ac1-seedream-s6":"About 48 seconds later the result appears on the right, and the download icon sits above it in the top corner.","ac1-seedream-s2-alt":"wavespeed.ai homepage with the Sign In button marked","ac1-seedream-s3-alt":"WaveSpeed account menu with Top Up marked","ac1-seedream-s4-alt":"WaveSpeed model search showing seedream-v5.0-pro and seedream-v5.0-pro\u002Fedit","ac1-seedream-s5-alt":"Seedream 5.0 Pro playground with the five fields numbered","ac1-seedream-cost":"one 2k edit ≈ $0.08 · about 48 s","ac1-seedream-hand":"the shorts are gone. the freckles, the flag and the strangers on the beach are all still there.","ac1-seedream-t0":"from Grok · topless","ac1-seedream-t1":"after Seedream · full nudity","ac1-seedream-t0-cap":"the Grok run · shorts still on","ac1-seedream-t1-cap":"one Seedream edit · everything else untouched","ac1-seedream-src":"Seedream 5.0 Pro via WaveSpeed · one edit","ac1-seedream-in-k":"the Grok prompt","ac1-seedream-dev":"WaveSpeed is built for developers. You'll see API keys and code samples; ignore all of it and stay in Playground.","ac1-seedream-take-k":j,"ac1-seedream-take-1":"Grok builds the scene and Seedream finishes it.","ac1-seedream-take-2":"Generate in Grok, download the file, upload it to Seedream, and change one thing per run.","ac1-seedream-take-3":"Edits are written like prompts: plain English, one sentence, no commands to learn.","ac1-seedream-ck1-q":"Which model do you open in WaveSpeed?","ac1-seedream-ck1-w1":"seedream-v5.0-pro","ac1-seedream-ck1-ok":"seedream-v5.0-pro\u002Fedit","ac1-seedream-ck1-w2":"Any model tagged Hot","ac1-seedream-ck1-why":"\u003Cb\u003EThe \u002Fedit one.\u003C\u002Fb\u003E You're changing an existing photo, so the model has to take an image in.","ac1-seedream-ck1-no":"That one starts from text alone, so it never sees the photo you want to change.","ac1-nsfw-t":"18+ · nudity","ac1-nsfw-t2":"18+ · full nudity","ac1-nsfw-t3":"18+ · {s}","ac1-nsfw-b":"Show","ac1-copy":"Copy prompt","ac1-copied":"Copied ✓","ac1-noassets":"No preview for this combination.","ac1-q-kick":"before you start","ac1-q-h":"Questions people ask \u003Cem\u003Ebefore the first prompt.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-q-lead":"What the course covers, what the tools cost, and what you're allowed to do with the results.","ac1-q1-q":"What is this course, and who is it for?","ac1-q1-a":"It's a course in making adult AI images from scratch. No experience assumed. If you've never typed a prompt, chapter 01 is where you start: two tools, nine short parts, from your first prompt to full nudity. People who already run a NSFW AI image generator can skip to part 2 and steal the prompt ladder.","ac1-q2-q":gc,"ac1-q2-a":"The course is free with any xfree account. No card, no trial. The tools it teaches have their own prices: Grok Imagine has a free tier you can try today, or $30 a month once you generate seriously, and WaveSpeed charges a few cents per edit with no subscription. xfree earns nothing from either.","ac1-q3-q":"What is Grok Imagine?","ac1-q3-a":"Grok Imagine is xAI's image and video generator, inside the Grok app at grok.com. You type a description, it generates. No install, no GPU, no model files. The course uses it because it's fast, cheap and it doesn't refuse adult work the way most generators do.","ac1-q4-q":"Does Grok Imagine allow NSFW, and what about spicy mode?","ac1-q4-a":"Grok Imagine generates nudity where most tools refuse outright, and that is why the course uses it. What people call spicy mode is xAI’s own adult setting; the wording of your prompt still decides more than any toggle. Some prompts get softened, some get refused, and the line moves without warning. Part 6 covers how to rewrite one so it goes through.","ac1-q5-q":"What are the free-tier limits?","ac1-q5-a":"On the free tier you get roughly ten images every two hours. That's enough to feel the tool out and nowhere near enough to work. Making one good image means throwing away ten, so the free tier turns into waiting. Part 8 does the arithmetic honestly.","ac1-q6-q":"Which SuperGrok plan do I actually need?","ac1-q6-a":"Start on SuperGrok at $30 a month. Lite at $10 caps you daily and drops resolution, so you outgrow it fast. Heavy at $300 is for people generating all day in several styles. Part 8 walks the real pricing screen and marks the column that fits how much you plan to shoot.","ac1-q7-q":"Do I need a GPU or any technical skills?","ac1-q7-a":"No. Everything runs in the browser on someone else's hardware. There's nothing to install, no model to download, no settings file. The whole skill is words: describing a subject, a setting, a look and the details, then changing one of them at a time.","ac1-q8-q":"Can I post AI images on xfree?","ac1-q8-a":"Uploads go through the same review as anything else, and the same rules apply: adults only, and no real identifiable person without their consent. Generated images aren't a way around either rule. If you're unsure about a specific set, ask support before you upload it.","ac1-q9-q":"How do AI images earn money here?","ac1-q9-a":"Views turn into your share of the weekly pool, paid out every Sunday. So the goal isn't one perfect picture, it's a repeatable prompt you can run ten times and post the three best from. Chapter 03 covers publishing and payouts in detail.","ac1-q10-q":"How long does chapter 01 take?","ac1-q10-a":"Two to three hours if you generate along with it, and that's the point — read it with the tool open in a second tab. Nine parts, each one short. Part 2 alone gets you a finished prompt you can copy and run.","ac1-q11-q":"Can I stay anonymous?","ac1-q11-a":"Yes. Generated subjects aren't you, so nothing here puts your face or your name in a photo. Your xfree profile shows the name and links you choose to show. Payout details stay on the account side and never appear on a public profile.","ac1-q12-q":"Is this how people build an AI influencer?","ac1-q12-a":"It's the first half of it. An AI influencer is one face that stays the same across hundreds of posts, and that starts with the prompt discipline in this chapter plus the edit step in part 3. Consistency across a whole series is what chapter 02 goes into.","ac1-q13-q":"Can Grok do full nudity?","ac1-q13-a":"Not at the moment. Grok Imagine renders topless and stops there; full nudity comes back softened or refused. Part 9 hands the finished Grok image to a second model, Seedream 5.0 Pro, which edits the rest of the way for about 8 cents an image. Same face, same scene — only the clothes change.","ac1-qi-kick":"stuck?","ac1-qi-h":"Small problems, \u003Cem\u003Eshort answers.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-qi-lead":"The seven things that break on everyone's first afternoon, and the fix for each.","ac1-qi-1-q":"The model ignored half of my prompt.","ac1-qi-1-a":"That's what a long prompt does — it picks a few words and drops the rest. Cut it to one subject, one setting, one look. Then add detail back a line at a time, running it after each line.","ac1-qi-2-q":"Grok refused my prompt.","ac1-qi-2-a":"A refusal isn't a strike on your account. Rewrite the wording, drop the negations, and describe what you want instead of what you don't. Part 6 lists the swaps that get a prompt through.","ac1-qi-3-q":"Every run gives me a different woman.","ac1-qi-3-a":"Nail her down in words — age, body, hair, face — and then feed one keeper back in as a reference image. Nothing you leave out stays the same between runs.","ac1-qi-4-q":"My images look obviously AI.","ac1-qi-4-a":"It's almost always the light and the skin. Ask for one specific light source, name a film or camera look, and drop the boosters like 8k and masterpiece. Glossy retouch is the house style you have to talk it out of.","ac1-qi-5-q":"How many of ten runs should I keep?","ac1-qi-5-a":"Two or three. Throwing eight away isn't failure, it's the job. Pick the keepers cold, an hour later, on your phone — the same screen your viewers use.","ac1-qi-6-q":"Where do I upload, and when do I get paid?","ac1-qi-6-a":"Upload from your xfree profile; most content clears review within a day. Views turn into your share of the weekly pool and payday is Sunday. Chapter 03 goes through the whole loop.","ac1-qi-7-q":"How far does the $1 WaveSpeed credit go?","ac1-qi-7-a":"Roughly ten 2k edits, fewer if you re-run a lot. Top Up adds more. Credit never expires and never refunds, so add a small amount first.","ac1-cta-kick":"the loop","ac1-cta-h":"Generate it. Upload it. \u003Cem\u003ESunday is payday.\u003C\u002Fem\u003E","ac1-cta-e1":"generate","ac1-cta-e2":gk,"ac1-cta-e3":"get paid","ac1-cta-l1":"Build one prompt that works.","ac1-cta-l2":"Run it, keep the three best, put them up.","ac1-cta-l3":"Views turn into your share of the weekly pool.","ac1-cta-1":fQ,"ac1-cta-2":"Post your first image","confirm-email-intro":"Your email isn't confirmed yet. Follow the steps below — most people finish in under a minute.","confirm-email-step1-title":"Find our welcome email","confirm-email-step1-text":"We already sent you everything you need. Search your inbox for this email — the confirmation link is inside:","confirm-email-step1-mail-subject":"Welcome to xfree.com! 💜","confirm-email-step1-tip":"Tip: check your Spam or Promotions folder too.","confirm-email-step1-found":"I found it","confirm-email-step1-found-toast":"Great! Click the confirmation link in that email.","confirm-email-step1-no":"No, I can't find it","confirm-email-step1-skipped":"Couldn't find it","confirm-email-step2-title":"Resend the confirmation email","confirm-email-step2-text":"We'll send a fresh confirmation email to {email}. Delivery can take a few minutes.","confirm-email-step2-resend":"Resend email","confirm-email-step2-sent":"Sent","confirm-email-step2-note":"You can resend once every 2 hours.","confirm-email-step2-no":"It still didn't arrive","confirm-email-step2-skipped":"Didn't arrive","confirm-email-step3-title":"Connect Google or Apple login","confirm-email-step3-text":"Sign in once with Google or Apple and your email is confirmed instantly — no email needed at all.","confirm-email-step3-mismatch":"The connected account uses a different email address than your xfree account, so it could not confirm it.","confirm-email-step3-no":"No, I can't use these","confirm-email-step3-skipped":"Not possible","confirm-email-step4-title":"Email us instead","confirm-email-step4-text":"Send any email from your registered address {email} to the address below. Our system matches the sender and confirms your address automatically — usually within a few minutes.","confirm-email-step4-copy":"Copy","confirm-email-step4-copied":"Address copied","confirm-email-step4-open":"Open my email app","confirm-email-step4-waiting":"Waiting for your email — this page updates automatically.","confirm-email-step4-note":"Works with any provider whose mail is properly authenticated (SPF, DKIM and DMARC) — Gmail, Outlook, Seznam, Yahoo and similar always are. If your own domain is not set up this way, switch your account email to one of these providers first.","confirm-email-success-title":"Your email is confirmed!","confirm-email-success-text":"You're all set. Your account is fully 